# Rust
/target
**/*.rs.bk
Cargo.lock.orig

# AgentOS runtime state. This repo self-hosts AgentOS: we TRACK the shared
# .agents/ policy content (*-policy.yaml, skills/) and ignore per-run
# operational artifacts AND per-machine state below. The work queue is
# runtime state, not config (82432d8); agentos.yaml holds a
# machine-generated workspace identity (workspace_id/created_at) plus personal
# preferences (default_access/max_parallel/auto_ime), so it is per-machine too
# (other repos may choose to track their own). workers.yaml is per-machine for
# the same reason: which CLIs are installed plus personal model/effort picks;
# `agentos init` regenerates it from templates::WORKERS, and untracking it
# keeps the parallel-mode git preflight green while you tune it.
/.agents/runs/
/.agents/resources/
/.agents/task-channels/
/.agents/checkpoints/
/.agents/handoffs/
/.agents/telemetry/
/.agents/transitions/
/.agents/intents/
/.agents/intent-contract.yaml
/.agents/work-queue.yaml
/.agents/conversations/
/.agents/git-finish-target.log
/.agents/approvals.yaml
/.agents/planning.lock
/.agents/locks/
/.agents/planning-sessions/
/.agents/activations/
/.agents/runtime-task-receipts/
/.agents/runtime-capability-receipts/
/.agents/activation-required.yaml
/.agents/gc-salvage/
/.agents/agentos.yaml
/.agents/workers.yaml

# Personal / per-machine harness files
*.local
.claude/settings.local.json
.codex/settings.local.json
.claude/worktrees/

# OS / editor
.DS_Store
*.swp
/.agents/worktrees/

# internal planning docs (kept local, not public)
docs/agentos-final-plan.md
docs/agentos-roadmap.md
docs/agentos-queue-ownership-design.md
